        "title": "feat(cloud): publish content-addressed review snapshots",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- publish complete Gitcrawl cloud-v2 snapshots from one exact source SQLite digest\n- stage snapshots without reader cutover when requested, then resume and cut over the same immutable snapshot later\n- preserve default reader cutover for existing publish callers\n- validate the complete writer and reader contract before any mutation, including `/query`, named queries, and exact argument schemas\n- hydrate pull-request files, observation-order metadata, coverage, and immutable snapshot provenance\n- scrub private source metadata before publication and pin crawlkit v0.14.0\n\n## Safety\n\n- snapshot IDs equal the lowercase SHA-256 of the source SQLite image\n- staged resume requires the exact snapshot capability set, source digest, schema, and coverage\n- malformed, stale, partial, or reader-incompatible remote contracts fail before publication or cutover\n- the final reader cutover remains gated on crawl-remote snapshot-provenance support\n\n## Validation\n\n- focused CLI and store tests passed\n- full GitHub matrix: 10/10 checks passed on `efe13645007ac0f72ecf5cc15715b765b6d6e1cc`\n- independent review repaired the missing reader-query preflight\n- final local ClawSweeper range review and cross-service staged/resume/cutover proof remain required before merge\n",
